extends RefCounted

const FLEE := "She opens the door, and the house lets her go.\n\nNo blade was drawn. No trap was set. No name was answered. Whatever waited at the center of that room — waiting to be ended, or answered, or understood — will wait there still, because Els Vantree decided that some other hand, some other night, could carry what she would not.\n\nThe house does not follow her into the dark outside. It doesn't need to. It has learned, the way it has learned every keeper before her: that fear is a kind of inheritance too, and she has just accepted hers in full.\n\nSomewhere behind her, a door that led to an ending closes on its own.\n\nShe will tell herself, later, that she was being careful. That leaving was wisdom, not weakness. But the house knows the difference, even if she never lets herself look at it directly again — and a woman who will not look at herself directly is not free. She has simply traded one kind of captivity for a quieter one, one she can carry in silence instead of stone.\n\nFreedom was standing in that room, waiting to be taken or ended. She chose neither. She chose the door.\n\nAnd a person who always chooses the door, when the room finally asks something of them — never becomes anything more than someone who is good at leaving."
const DESTROY := "Congratulations, brave one.\n\nThe Hound is dead. The bond is broken.\nNo next keeper."
